// ReplaySketch Scenario Profile — Alpine Assault: USA vs GLA (Full Build-Out)
// =============================================================================
//
// Variant of alpine-assault-usa-vs-gla.json that builds one of every buildable
// structure and trains one of every trainable unit for each faction (see
// BuildingCatalog.cs / UnitCatalog.cs for the authoritative per-faction lists),
// then only attacks once everything has finished. The original profile is left
// untouched so its hardcoded-action-count tests keep working.
//
// ─── DESIGN NOTES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Each player's actions form ONE strictly linear chain:
//   Gather Resources -> Building 1 -> Building 2 -> ... -> Building N
//     -> Unit 1 -> Unit 2 -> ... -> Unit M -> Attack Enemy Base
//
// Buildings are chained on the PREVIOUS building's "Completed" phase (with a
// short extraFrames buffer) so construction never overlaps and each build order
// only fires once there has been time to bank more credits. Because every
// building finishes before any unit is queued, prerequisite producer buildings
// (Barracks for infantry, War Factory / Arms Dealer for vehicles, Airfield for
// air units) are always already standing by the time their unit is recruited,
// without needing per-unit prerequisite tracking.
//
// Resource gathering starts as soon as the FIRST building's order is dispatched
// (same pattern as the standard scenario), giving the supply truck the maximum
// possible runway to fund the rest of the build-out from the 10000 starting
// credits plus trickle income over the scenario's ~10 minute (18000 frame)
// timeout budget (see HarnessRunner.DefaultFrameTimeout).
//
// Every RecruitBasicUnit action sets "quantity": 1 (one of each unit, not the
// standard scenario's default of 5 attackers).
//
// AttackEnemyBase is triggered by the very LAST unit's "Completed" phase, so it
// literally cannot fire until every building and every unit exists.
//
